      "answers": [
        "Date",
        "Location",
        "Server",
        "The HTTP status line"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": 1,
      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Maya:</b> One request to the site returned this response. Which field tells us where the client was directed?\n\n<b>HTTP/1.1 302 Found\nLocation: https://expose-login.freepress-check.com/login\nDate: 2025-07-14T10:12:37Z\nServer: mock-httpd/1.0</b>",
      "taskInstructions": "Review the Cyberpedia guidance on an <b>HTTP redirect</b>.",
      "taskQuestion": "Which header names the redirect destination?",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Maya:</b> The Location header names the next URL. The 302 status indicates a redirect response; neither field identifies who configured it."
    }
  ],
